# Ship through main

Every completed change that should go live follows this pipeline. Do not stop at push or an open PR.

1. `git fetch origin main` and merge/rebase onto latest `origin/main` before pushing.
2. If `LARAVEL_BACKEND/resources/` changed, run `cd LARAVEL_BACKEND && npm run build` and commit `public/build`.
3. Push the feature branch and open a PR targeting `main`.
4. Merge the PR into `main`.
5. Deploy production branch `main` via `POST https://relayiq.app/deploy/agent` with `X-Deploy-Agent-Key` from `LARAVEL_BACKEND/.env`.

Default deploy target is always `main`. Only skip the deploy step if the developer named a different branch or said not to deploy.
